      "portalId": "3323786a-68b2-4001-ae90-ec1ab84e7687",
      "title": "Lesson 30 : The Naib Al-Fā’il (Substitute of the Fā’il)",
      "overview": "In this video, we discuss the nāib al-fā’il. The المفعول الذي لم يُسَمَّ فاعله is a noun that replaces the omitted doer (fāʿil). It becomes marfūʿ after being manṣūb. The fāʿil is omitted due to ignorance, fear, respect, or brevity.\nAll fāʿil rules apply to the nāʾib al-fāʿil. The verb agrees in femininity but not in duality or plurality. In the past tense, the first letter has ḍammah and the one before last kasrah (ضُرِبَ); in the present, ḍammah then fatḥah (يُضرَبُ). Other forms include تُعُلِّمَ، اُستُخرِجَ، قِيلَ، قُولَ.\nThe nāʾib al-fāʿil can be:\nMafʿūl bihi (ضُرِبَ زيدٌ),\n\nẒarf (صِيمَ رمضانُ),\n\nJār–majrūr (سُقِطَ في أيديهم), or\n\nMaṣdar (نُفِخَ في الصور نفخةٌ).\n\nUsually, if the mafʿūl bihi exists, nothing else replaces it. If there are two mafʿūls, one becomes the nāʾib (أُعْطِيَ زيدٌ درهمًا).",
