      "portalId": "f91c97a8-79ec-44ad-911d-294d9993b313",
      "title": "Lesson 38 : Ẓanna and its Sisters",
      "overview": "In this video, we discuss ظن and its sisters. These verbs turn the mubtada and khabar into two maf‘ūls, like ظننتُ زيدًا قائمًا. They are called أفعال القلوب because they deal with belief or assumption. Some indicate certainty, some probability, and some can mean either. If ظن means “accuse,” رأى means “see,” or علم means “know,” they only take one maf‘ūl.\nA related group, أفعال التّصْيير (جعل، ردّ، اتخذ، صيّر، وهب), make one thing into another, like جعلتُ الطينَ خزفًا. جعل can mean beginning, creating, believing, or transforming. هبْ and تعلّمْ (in the sense of “know X to be Y”) are only used in the amr form.\nThese verbs may work normally (ʿamal), be cancelled (ilghā’) if delayed, or be suspended (ta‘līq) when something like لام الابتداء or استفهام enters. Ta‘līq and ilghā’ do not apply to af‘āl al-taṣyīr nor to the jāmid forms هب and تعلّم.\nBoth maf‘ūls can be omitted if context shows them. Some include سمعتُ among these verbs, but most say it normally has one maf‘ūl and the following sentence is ḥāl or ṣifah depending on the noun.",
